# Cloudflare Pages headers (the origin since the 2026-08-02 cutover — .htaccess is dead here).
# Security baseline per docs/optimization-backlog.md §12.1 and docs/ux-cro-security.md §5.
# HSTS deliberately WITHOUT includeSubDomains (mail/webmail subdomains not guaranteed HTTPS)
# and WITHOUT preload (near-irreversible — owner's call, docs/business-facts.md §F).
#
# CSP is REPORT-ONLY on purpose. Shipping it now, BEFORE any analytics lands, is deliberate:
# the site currently has zero third-party scripts, so the strictest possible policy costs nothing
# to state and establishes the baseline. Installing a tag manager later will require widening
# script-src (and adding frame-src) — do that in the SAME commit as the tag, never after.
# Promote to enforcing (drop "-Report-Only") only after a full week of real traffic, including a
# real form submission, produces no legitimate violations.
#   'unsafe-inline' in style-src: Next emits inline styles; removing it costs more than it returns.
#   imgquarry.com in connect-src (2026-10-12, same change as the script that needs it):
#   /assets/live.js reads the fleet status switch, https://imgquarry.com/status/fleet.json, once
#   per page view (CLAUDE.md §14). Blocked, the switch reads as unreadable and every seasonal line
#   and the card stay off — silently. The live surfaces' two inline <head> scripts are covered by
#   the existing 'unsafe-inline', /assets/live.js by 'self'.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://www.googletagmanager.com; connect-src 'self' https://www.google-analytics.com https://*.analytics.google.com https://*.googletagmanager.com https://imgquarry.com; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://www.google-analytics.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-src https://www.googletagmanager.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'

# The production pages.dev alias serves the whole site as an indexable 200 duplicate (measured
# 2026-10-19). This absolute-URL rule is Cloudflare's documented fix and matches on the request HOST,
# so thermoleak.co.il and www are untouched. Preview deployments already send noindex by default.
# After a deploy: `curl -sI https://thermoleak.pages.dev/` shows X-Robots-Tag: noindex, and
# `curl -sI https://thermoleak.co.il/` shows NO X-Robots-Tag — if it does, roll back at once.
https://:project.pages.dev/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Fingerprinted build assets are immutable by construction.
/_next/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# /images/* is NOT content-hashed — hero.webp and thermoleak_logo.webp keep their names across
# deploys — so `immutable` would be wrong: a corrected image could stay cached for a year with no
# way to bust it. 30 days with normal revalidation is the right trade, and the invalidation path is
# rename-on-change (docs/performance-guidelines.md §5). Without this rule both files revalidate off
# a Cloudflare zone default that this repo does not control.
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
